# Crystal Imperium play test: Rare Candies several at a time (DECISIONS.md D33). After choosing the
# Pokemon, the party menu asks how many to use, at first all the levels up to the cap (UP/DOWN 1,
# LEFT/RIGHT 10). They are used at once, with one message and a short sound instead of the
# level-up fanfare (sFanfareCounter stays 0, so the map music goes on), and without the two stat
# pages: one A after the message is back at choosing a Pokemon. The moves of every level passed
# are learned, and the Pokemon evolves at the end; at the cap, a Rare Candy still evolves a Pokemon
# that can evolve.
# Magikarp learns nothing from 6 to 14 (Tackle at 15); Caterpie learns Bug Bite at 9 and evolves
# at 7. The level cap is 15 with no badges.
!new_game()
!give_mon(129, 5)
!give_mon(10, 5)
!use_key_item(0)
!open_bag_at("POCKET_MEDICINE", 0)
press A
wait 20
press A
wait 120

# Magikarp: up to 10, one less with DOWN, used at once
press A
wait 60
shot 01_how_many.png
expect16 {sRareCandyCount} 10 count_starts_at_the_cap
press DOWN
wait 10
expect16 {sRareCandyCount} 9 down_takes_one_off
press A
wait 30
expect16 {sFanfareCounter} 0 no_level_up_fanfare
expect8 {gPlayerParty+84} 14 nine_levels_at_once
wait 90
shot 02_elevated_to_14.png
press A
wait 60
# No stat pages: this A already chooses Magikarp again. One level is left, so no question
press A
wait 60
expect8 {gPlayerParty+84} 15 one_more_without_asking
shot 03_elevated_to_15.png
# "elevated to Lv. 15", "MAGIKARP learned TACKLE!", back to choosing a Pokemon
press A
wait 120
press A
wait 120

# Caterpie: B in the question uses none; then all 10 at once: it learns Bug Bite on the way, then
# evolves into Metapod
press DOWN
wait 20
press A
wait 60
press B
wait 60
expect8 {gPlayerParty+184} 5 b_uses_no_rare_candy
press A
wait 60
expect16 {sRareCandyCount} 10 caterpie_count_starts_at_the_cap
press A
wait 30
expect8 {gPlayerParty+184} 15 caterpie_ten_levels_at_once
waituntil32 {gMain+4} {CB2_EvolutionSceneUpdate+1} 900 A caterpie_evolves
shot 04_evolving.png
waituntil32 {gMain+4} {CB2_UpdatePartyMenu+1} 3000 A back_in_the_party_menu
expect8 {gPlayerParty+184} 15 metapod_at_15
wait 60
shot 05_back_in_party_menu.png

# At the cap a Rare Candy gives no level, but a Pokemon that can evolve still does (one candy):
# Metapod (level 10) into Butterfree
press A
waituntil32 {gMain+4} {CB2_EvolutionSceneUpdate+1} 900 A metapod_evolves_at_the_cap
waituntil32 {gMain+4} {CB2_UpdatePartyMenu+1} 3000 A back_after_butterfree
expect8 {gPlayerParty+184} 15 butterfree_still_at_15
shot 06_after_butterfree.png
